_🗄️ Data Integrity & Integration_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**`parseAtomicUnits` accepts values above `u64::MAX`.**

The regex `^(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,19})$` permits 20 digits, so the maximum accepted value is `99999999999999999999`. `u64::MAX` is `18446744073709551615`. The error message states "unsigned base-10 u64 integer string", but values up to five times that bound pass. These amounts reach the Anchor paymaster, which stores `u64` token amounts, so the overflow surfaces later as a truncation or a program abort instead of a rejected manifest.

Check the numeric bound after parsing.

<details>
<summary>🐛 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
+const U64_MAX = 18_446_744_073_709_551_615n;
+
 export function parseAtomicUnits(value: string, field: string): bigint {
-  if (!/^(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,19})$/.test(value)) {
+  if (!/^(0|[1-9][0-9]{0,19})$/.test(value)) {
     throw new Error(`${field} must be an unsigned base-10 u64 integer string`);
   }
-  return BigInt(value);
+  const parsed = BigInt(value);
+  if (parsed > U64_MAX) {
+    throw new Error(`${field} must be an unsigned base-10 u64 integer string`);
+  }
+  return parsed;
 }
```
</details>

