_🔒 Security & Privacy_ | _🟠 Major_ | _⚡ Quick win_

**An unparsable `expiresAt` bypasses the expiry check.**

`Date.parse` returns `NaN` for a malformed or empty `expiresAt`. Every comparison with `NaN` is false, so the guard passes and an expired or untimed receipt is accepted. Reject a non-finite timestamp explicitly.

<details>
<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-  if (Date.parse(receipt.expiresAt) <= now.getTime()) {
+  const expiresAt = Date.parse(receipt.expiresAt);
+  if (!Number.isFinite(expiresAt)) {
+    throw new Error('SIGN_RECEIPT_EXPIRY_INVALID');
+  }
+  if (expiresAt <= now.getTime()) {
     throw new Error('SIGN_RECEIPT_EXPIRED');
   }
```
</details>

